# Fork GitHub boundary

This checkout is the **detroitpro/t3code** fork. Personal work is tracked here only.

## Hard rule

**Never** use `https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code` (or `pingdotgg/t3code`) for:

- `gh` / GitHub API (`-R`, clone URLs for issues/PRs, discussion create/comment)
- Opening or linking issues, PRs, discussions, or release pages in replies
- Prefill `issues/new` URLs, Ideas discussions, or triage filing
- Docs, README, CONTRIBUTING, playbooks, or agent guidance you edit (except the
  fetch-only sync notes in `FORK.md` / `merge-upstream`)

**Always** use `https://github.com/detroitpro/t3code` (or `detroitpro/t3code` / `origin`).

## `gh` must not leave the fork

- **Never** add a permanent git remote named `upstream` (or any remote whose URL
  is the other GitHub copy). A named `upstream` remote makes `gh pr create`
  open PRs against that repo by default.
- Every `gh` call that needs a repo must pass **`--repo detroitpro/t3code`**
  (or `-R detroitpro/t3code`). Do not rely on ambient resolution.
- After clone/bootstrap: `gh repo set-default detroitpro/t3code` so
  `remote.origin.gh-resolved=base` is set locally.

## Allowed exception (git fetch only)

When the user asks to sync a **stable release**, fetch tags/commits with a
**one-shot URL** (no lasting remote), then cherry-pick into this fork. See
`merge-upstream` / `FORK.md`. Never push to that URL, and never use its GitHub
UI/API.

## If you already targeted the wrong GitHub copy

1. Stop.
2. Retract or redirect to the equivalent `detroitpro/t3code` artifact.
3. Prefer creating the correct issue/PR/discussion on the fork immediately.
